WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:06.034
Step five makes a folder for the inventory
and runs the guide's four Step 2 queries,

2
00:00:06.034 --> 00:00:10.320
writing each to a J SON file:
public I Ps, Front Door profiles,

3
00:00:10.320 --> 00:00:14.250
application gateways, and
pass with public access on.

4
00:00:14.250 --> 00:00:16.712
The full commands are on the module page.

5
00:00:16.712 --> 00:00:19.887
Step six finds the public
I Ps with no owner.

6
00:00:19.887 --> 00:00:24.342
That filter is the path's own, not the
guide's: it reads the data array that

7
00:00:24.342 --> 00:00:29.412
the Resource Graph extension writes, and
keeps the rows whose owner tag is empty.

8
00:00:29.412 --> 00:00:33.024
The guide's Validate step says
every row should have an owner,

9
00:00:33.024 --> 00:00:35.551
or each ownerless row
should have a ticket.

10
00:00:35.551 --> 00:00:39.612
Module 5 counts these rows
again, to compute the metrics.

11
00:00:39.612 --> 00:00:41.237
Step seven backs it out.

12
00:00:41.237 --> 00:00:44.654
The lab created nothing in
Azure, but the out folder is a

13
00:00:44.654 --> 00:00:48.360
map of the test subscription's
attack surface, so delete it.
